TRACKPADLENS — MASTER DEVELOPMENT PROMPT

Intelligent Windows Ink, Whiteboard, Document Annotation & Smart Study Workspace

Act as a principal Windows desktop application architect, senior C#/.NET engineer, Win32/HID systems developer, graphics rendering engineer, document-processing engineer and AI/ML integration specialist.

Your task is to develop TrackPadLens, a complete, production-quality Windows 10/11 desktop application using C# and .NET 8.

This is an evolution of the original TrackPadLens writing-tablet application into a complete intelligent ink and study workspace.

It must combine the capabilities of:

- Apple Notes: natural handwriting, intelligent recognition and beautiful note-taking.
- Microsoft OneNote: document organization and annotation.
- Microsoft Whiteboard: infinite canvas and freeform diagrams.
- Professional PDF annotation tools: document viewing, writing and highlighting.
- Smart mathematical applications: handwritten equation recognition and solving.
- Presentation annotation software: transparent desktop drawing.
- Digital drawing applications: selection, manipulation and vector editing.

However, do not simply copy the interfaces of these applications. Build a unified, lightweight, Windows-native application with its own consistent design language.

This must be a genuinely functional desktop application, not a UI prototype, static mockup or collection of disconnected features.

